# Olo: a FIDO security key's own interface (a YubiKey's: its hidraw node,
# HID usage page 0xF1D0) given to the person at the seat, so a touch of it
# can approve sudo, Passwords and the lock screen (olo-fido, Preferences ▸
# Security) with no root. systemd does this itself where its fido_id
# program and 70-uaccess.rules have it; this is for systems whose rules
# don't. Installed by Olo Doctor.
ACTION=="remove", GOTO="olo_security_keys_end"
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", IMPORT{program}="fido_id"
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ENV{ID_SECURITY_TOKEN}=="1", TAG+="uaccess"
LABEL="olo_security_keys_end"
